  76	    /// A change counter for anything that can affect how images are
  77	    /// drawn. It changes when images or placements are added, removed,
  78	    /// or modified, and also when placements move on screen without
  79	    /// changing, such as during scrolling, resizing, or erasing history.
  80	    ///
  81	    /// The counter is never reset. Instead, each consumer keeps the last
  82	    /// value it saw and compares it to the current value. Because nothing
  83	    /// clears the counter, any number of consumers can watch the same
  84	    /// storage independently. Within Ghostty, only `RenderState` reads
  85	    /// it, to know when to position its placements again. A renderer
  86	    /// should watch `RenderState.imagePlacementsGeneration` instead. For
  87	    /// example, a consumer of the storage would do:
  88	    ///
  89	    ///     if (storage.dirty != self.last_dirty) {
  90	    ///         self.last_dirty = storage.dirty;
  91	    ///         self.rebuildPlacements(storage);
  92	    ///     }
  93	    ///
  94	    /// Only compare values for equality. The counter wraps around on
  95	    /// overflow, so "greater than" has no meaning.
  96	    ///
  97	    /// The difference from `generation` is that `generation` only
  98	    /// changes when the contents change. Every change to `generation`
  99	    /// also changes `dirty`, so if `dirty` changed but `generation` did
 100	    /// not, the images and placements are the same and only their
 101	    /// positions on screen may have moved.
 102	    ///
 103	    /// Update this with `markDirty` or `markMutated` rather than writing
 104	    /// it directly. There are two exceptions. `Terminal.switchScreen`
 105	    /// sets the new screen's counter past the old screen's so that a
 106	    /// consumer can never see the same value on both screens, and
 107	    /// `Screen.reset` carries the counter over to the new storage.
 108	    dirty: u64 = 0,
 109	
 110	    /// Generation stamp of the last content mutation to this storage:
 111	    /// any image transmit/replace, placement add, or delete of either.
 112	    /// Zero means the storage has never been mutated (and is therefore
 113	    /// empty).
 114	    ///
 115	    /// Unlike dirty, this is NOT updated by scrolling/resizing, so an
 116	    /// unchanged generation means the placement set and all image data
 117	    /// are identical; only placement geometry (pins) may have moved.
 118	    /// Values come from a process-global monotonic counter, so a value
 119	    /// observed from any storage never recurs for different content,
 120	    /// even across screen switches or storage resets.
