  78	    /// or modified, and also when placements move on screen without
  79	    /// changing, such as during scrolling, resizing, or erasing history.
  80	    ///
  81	    /// The counter is never reset. Instead, each consumer keeps the last
  82	    /// value it saw and compares it to the current value. Because nothing
  83	    /// clears the counter, any number of consumers can watch the same
  84	    /// storage independently. Within Ghostty, only `RenderState` reads
  85	    /// it, to know when to position its placements again. A renderer
  86	    /// should watch `RenderState.imagePlacementsGeneration` instead. For
  87	    /// example, a consumer of the storage would do:
  88	    ///
  89	    ///     if (storage.dirty != self.last_dirty) {
  90	    ///         self.last_dirty = storage.dirty;
  91	    ///         self.rebuildPlacements(storage);
  92	    ///     }
  93	    ///
  94	    /// Only compare values for equality. The counter wraps around on
  95	    /// overflow, so "greater than" has no meaning.
  96	    ///
  97	    /// The difference from `generation` is that `generation` only
  98	    /// changes when the contents change. Every change to `generation`
  99	    /// also changes `dirty`, so if `dirty` changed but `generation` did
